---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Design Lab
description: Build a system design by dragging components onto a canvas for a real interview scenario, then get it rated with feedback and see the best design.
section: lab
permalink: /lab/
pageScripts: ["/assets/js/lab.js"]
---
<div class="lab">
  <p class="eyebrow">Practice · interactive</p>
  <h1>Design Lab</h1>
  <p class="lede">Pick a scenario, drag components onto the canvas and connect them. Then check your design: you'll get a rank, what you got right, what's missing and why, and the design an interviewer would hope to see.</p>

  <div class="lab__bar">
    <label class="visually-hidden" for="lab-scenario">Scenario</label>
    <select class="fc-select lab__scenario" id="lab-scenario" data-lab-scenario>
      {%- for s in lab.scenarios %}
      <option value="{{ s.id }}">{{ s.title }} · {{ s.level }}</option>
      {%- endfor %}
    </select>
    <button class="btn btn--berry" type="button" data-lab-check>Check my design</button>
    <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" data-lab-model>Show the best design</button>
    <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" data-lab-clear>Clear</button>
  </div>

  {%- for s in lab.scenarios %}
  <div class="lab__brief" data-brief="{{ s.id }}"{% if not loop.first %} hidden{% endif %}>
    <p class="lab__brief-title">The brief</p>
    <ul>{% for b in s.brief %}<li>{{ b | md | safe }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
    {%- if s.walkthrough %}<p class="lab__brief-link">Full walkthrough: <a href="{{ s.walkthrough }}">{{ s.title }}</a> (try the lab first!)</p>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {%- endfor %}

  <div class="lab__work">
    <div class="lab__palette" aria-label="Components">
      <p class="lab__palette-title">Components</p>
      <p class="lab__tip">Drag onto the canvas, or tap to add.</p>
      <div class="lab__chips">
        {%- for c in lab.components %}
        <button class="lab__chip d-node--{{ c.kind }}" type="button" data-type="{{ c.t }}" title="{{ c.hint }}">{{ c.icon | safe }}<span>{{ c.label }}</span></button>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="lab__canvas" data-lab-canvas aria-label="Design canvas">
      <svg class="lab__edges" aria-hidden="true">
        <defs><marker id="lab-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z"/></marker></defs>
        <g data-lab-edges></g>
        <line class="lab__temp" data-lab-temp hidden/>
      </svg>
      <p class="lab__empty" data-lab-empty><span>Drag components here.<br>Then pull from a box's <b>●</b> handle to another box to connect them.</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="lab__connect">
    <span class="lab__connect-label">Connect</span>
    <label class="visually-hidden" for="lab-from">From</label>
    <select class="fc-select" id="lab-from" data-lab-from></select>
    <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <label class="visually-hidden" for="lab-to">To</label>
    <select class="fc-select" id="lab-to" data-lab-to></select>
    <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" data-lab-link>Add link</button>
    <span class="lab__tip">Click a line to remove it. Your canvas is saved in this browser.</span>
  </div>

  <section class="calc" aria-labelledby="calc-title">
    <h2 id="calc-title">Capacity calculator</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">How big does this design need to be? Set the traffic and the work each request does; the calculator sizes the servers, load balancers, database, cache and workers. It reads your canvas too: the database and load balancer you picked, and whether there's a cache.</p>
    <div class="calc__grid">
      <form class="calc__form" data-calc-form onsubmit="return false">
        <fieldset>
          <legend>Traffic</legend>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>Daily active users</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="dau"><span class="calc__unit"></span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>Requests per user per day</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="rpu"><span class="calc__unit"></span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>Peak ÷ average</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="peak"><span class="calc__unit">×</span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>Served by CDN / edge</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="edge"><span class="calc__unit">%</span></span></label>
        </fieldset>
        <fieldset>
          <legend>Work per request</legend>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>CPU time</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="cpuMs"><span class="calc__unit">ms</span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>Response time</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="respMs"><span class="calc__unit">ms</span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>Memory while in flight</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="mbReq"><span class="calc__unit">MB</span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>Target CPU use</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="util"><span class="calc__unit">%</span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>Server size</span><span class="calc__in"><select data-calc="size">
            <option value="auto">Auto: pick for me</option>
            <option value="2">2 vCPU · 4 GB</option>
            <option value="4">4 vCPU · 8 GB</option>
            <option value="8">8 vCPU · 16 GB</option>
            <option value="16">16 vCPU · 32 GB</option>
            <option value="32">32 vCPU · 64 GB</option>
            <option value="64">64 vCPU · 128 GB</option>
          </select></span></label>
        </fieldset>
        <fieldset>
          <legend>Data</legend>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>DB reads per request</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="reads"><span class="calc__unit"></span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>Cache hit rate</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="hit"><span class="calc__unit">%</span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>New DB records per day</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="recDay"><span class="calc__unit"></span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>Record size</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="recBytes"><span class="calc__unit">bytes</span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>Keep data for</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="years"><span class="calc__unit">years</span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>Copies of each record</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="rf"><span class="calc__unit">×</span></span></label>
        </fieldset>
        <fieldset>
          <legend>Files, jobs and connections</legend>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>New files per day</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="filesDay"><span class="calc__unit"></span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>File size</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="fileMB"><span class="calc__unit">MB</span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>Background jobs per day</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="jobsDay"><span class="calc__unit"></span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>CPU per job</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="jobCpuS"><span class="calc__unit">s</span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>Open connections (WebSockets)</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="conns"><span class="calc__unit"></span></span></label>
        </fieldset>
        <details class="calc__assume">
          <summary>Assumptions</summary>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>L7 load balancer, requests/s each</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="l7rps"><span class="calc__unit"></span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>L4 load balancer, requests/s each</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="l4rps"><span class="calc__unit"></span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>Connections per realtime gateway</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="connsPerGw"><span class="calc__unit"></span></span></label>
          <label class="calc__field"><span>Usable GB per Redis node</span><span class="calc__in"><input type="number" min="0" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-calc="redisGB"><span class="calc__unit"></span></span></label>
          <p class="calc__note">Database limits per node depend on the database you pick on the canvas (for example PostgreSQL ≈ 5k writes/s per primary, Cassandra ≈ 10k writes/s per node). They're rough planning numbers, not benchmarks.</p>
        </details>
        <p><button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" data-calc-reset>Reset to this scenario's numbers</button></p>
      </form>
      <div class="calc__side">
        <div class="guess" data-guess>
          <p class="guess__title">Your estimate first</p>
          <p class="guess__lede">How many of each will this design need at peak? Guess, then reveal. Way too many and it <b>blasts</b> (wasted money); way too few and it <b>melts down</b> (overloaded).</p>
          <div class="guess__fields" data-guess-fields></div>
          <div class="guess__btns">
            <button class="btn btn--berry" type="button" data-guess-reveal>Reveal</button>
            <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" data-guess-skip>Just show me</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="calc__out" data-calc-out aria-live="polite" hidden></div>
        <p class="guess__again" hidden><button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" data-guess-again>Guess again</button></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="lab__result" data-lab-result hidden aria-live="polite"></section>

  {%- for s in lab.scenarios %}
  <section class="lab__model" data-model="{{ s.id }}" hidden>
    <h2>The best design: {{ s.title }}</h2>
    {{ s.model.spec | diagram(s.model.caption) | safe }}
    <ul class="lab__notes">{% for n in s.notes %}<li>{{ n | md | safe }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
    {%- if s.walkthrough %}<p><a class="btn" href="{{ s.walkthrough }}">Read the full walkthrough</a></p>{% endif %}
  </section>
  {%- endfor %}
</div>
<script id="lab-data" type="application/json">{{ lab | labJson | safe }}</script>
